Package: ff802-cc
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Bernhard Steinheber <bernhard@steinheber.info>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libusb-1.0-0 (>= 2:1.0.22)
Suggests: ff802-cc-auto, ff802-ucm-profile
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Description: manual USB mode switch for the original RME Fireface 802
 ff802-cc switches an original RME Fireface 802 (not the 802 FS) by hand
 between proprietary USB mode (2a39:3fcd) and class-compliant mode
 (0424:3fdd), after an interactive confirmation:
 .
  sudo ff802-cc enable    proprietary -> class-compliant, then resets the
                          USB hub port of the unit
  sudo ff802-cc disable   class-compliant -> proprietary
 .
 ff802-detect lists the unit and its mode without opening it.
 .
 Independent of ff802-cc-auto (the automatic switch at connection) and of
 ff802-ucm-profile (the audio configuration); disable is refused while
 ff802-cc-auto is on. No udev rule, no service, no maintainer script.
